      "sequence_position": 11,
      "problem": "Given that $9{t}^{2}+30t+25=0,$ what are the values of $t?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the left-hand side is a perfect square. It just needs to be factored:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{t}^{2}+30t+25 & =0 \\\\ (3t)^{2}+2\\cdot 3t\\cdot 5+{5}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (3t+5)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(3t+5)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{0} \\\\ |3t+5| & =0 \\\\ 3t+5 & =0 \\\\ 3t & =-5 \\\\ t & =-\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
